  "question": {
    "text": "The heat of combustion of ethanol into carbon dioxides and water is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>327</mn></math>&nbsp;Kcal at constant pressure. The heat evolved (in cal) at constant volume at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>27</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> (if all gases behave ideally) is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>calmol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math>________",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "326400",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mi>OH</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>&#8467;</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#10230;</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>&#8467;</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>;</mo><mi>&#916;</mi><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>327</mn><mi>Kcal</mi></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>Hc</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#916;</mi><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">U</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>&#916;</mi><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></msub><mi>RT</mi></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>327</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>&#916;</mi><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">U</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>300</mn></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;</mi><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">U</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>326400</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cal</mi></math></p><p>So heat evolved as constant volume is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>326400</mn></math>cal&nbsp;</p>",
